    <selectionEntry id="f670-7544-e4f3-f5fa" name="Argyrum-pattern Boarding Shield" hidden="true" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="false">
          <conditionGroups>
            <conditionGroup type="or">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="equalTo" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="8e0f-3552-8842-f281" shared="true" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false"/>
                <condition type="instanceOf" value="1" field="selections" scope="ancestor" childId="3cd1-f7ee-0b1e-bd47" shared="true" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false"/>
              </conditions>
            </conditionGroup>
          </conditionGroups>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <profiles>
        <profile id="de24-f317-3b22-4a32" name="Argyrum pattern boarding shield" hidden="false" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">An Argyrum pattern boarding shield provides a 5+ Invulnerable Save against Shooting Attacks in any Phase that increases to 4+ against any attacks made while engaged in an assault. Invulnerable Saves granted by an Argyrum pattern boarding shield do not stack with other Invulnerable Saves and cannot be modified by any other special rule. If a model has another Invulnerable Save then the controlling player must choose which one to use. In addition, a model with has another Invulnerable Save then the controlling player must choose which one to use. In addition, a model with an Argyrum pattern boarding shield may not make attacks with any weapon that has the Two-handed special rule.|
An Argyrum Pattern Boarding Shield counts as a Boarding Shield for all intents and purposes, including Rites of War, Special Rules, and wargear limitations which either require their use or prevent it (such as a Master of Signals being prevented from taking a Boarding Shield), though it does not confer any of the benefits normally gained from a Boarding Shield from any such sources. 
In addition, a model armed with an Argyrum Pattern Boarding Shield cannot claim bonus attacks for having more than one melee weapon.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
